  "question": {
    "text": "An LCR circuit is equivalent to a damped pendulum. In an LCR circuit the capacitor is charged to <math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> and then connected to the L and R as shown below:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0155_146bbd7763fb.png\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 165px;\" /><br />If a student plots graphs of the square of maximum charge <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfenced></math> on the capacitor with time (t) for two different values <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> of L then which of the following represents this graph correctly? (plots are schematic and not drawn to scale)"
  },
